CORE
main.py
--python-check-annotations --unwind 3 --no-unwinding-assertions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\[annotation-mismatch
--
Opt-in --python-check-annotations FALSE POSITIVE (not a false proof). DESIRED
behaviour (encoded above): an Any-valued dict annotation (`dict[str, Any]`)
should NOT raise an annotation-mismatch, so the program verifies SUCCESSFUL.
CURRENT behaviour: `dict[str, Any]` lowers to int (the dict-value non-"safe"
fallback in convert_type_annotation), the checker reads that as a precise `int`
declaration and flags the dict literal -> VERIFICATION FAILED. The principled
fix (Any-valued dict -> python_dict with python_value values) is blocked by a
separate Any-valued-CONTAINER capacity-model-bound issue (typing the values as
Any makes `d[k].append(...)` hit [python-model-bound]; see dict-if-not-in-idiom,
the architecture-doc master inventory section A, and plan §7). When that
representation issue is fixed this test should start passing -> promote to CORE.
